    <rdfs:label>arginine vasopressin</rdfs:label>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A gene, transcript, or peptide form of arginine vasopressin, a hormone produced in neurons of the hypothalamus and released from vesicles into the circulation in response to extracellular fluid hypertonicity. It primarily functions to increase the amount of solute-free water reabsorbed back into the circulation from the filtrate in the kidney tubules of nephrons and to constrict artertioles, which increases peripheral vascular resistance and raises arterial blood pressure.</obo:IAO_0000115>
    <craft:annotatable_text>8-arginine-vasopressin; 8-L-arginine vasopressin; [Arg8]-vasopressin; arginine vasopressin; argipressin; AVP; AVP-NPII</craft:annotatable_text>
  </owl:Class>
